   =20

 =20
 =20
                  <p>Baddy Sonja Breidert is the CEO and Co-Founder of 1xIN=
TERNET,&nbsp;a growing Drupal company in Frankfurt, Germany, Conil, Spain a=
nd Reykjav=C3=ADk, Iceland.<br>
She graduated with a B.Sc. in Computer Science from the University of Reykj=
avik in 2003 and after that completed her M.Sc. in<br>
Engineering Management from the Technical University in Vienna, where she t=
oday teaches Agile Project management and IT.</p>

<p>Baddy has been an active member in the Drupal Community since 2013 and i=
s one of the board members at Drupal Association.&nbsp; Baddy took part in =
organising Drupal Europe and is known to really understand both business an=
d open source and believes both are empowering each other and could even be=
 a necessity.&nbsp;</p>

         =20
 =20


  </div>

  <div class=3D"speaker--sessions">
  <a name=3D"talk" class=3D"visually-hidden"></a>
  <h2 class=3D"title title-shape-green">
        Talks  </h2>
  <ul>
      <li>
     =20
<article role=3D"article" class=3D"node node--type--session node--view-mode=
--embed">
  <div class=3D"session--content">
   =20
    <h3><span class=3D"field field--name-title field--type-string field--la=
bel-hidden">Drupal Association - Ask-Me-Anything</span>
</h3>
   =20
   =20

 =20
 =20
                  <p>An open dialogue with the Drupal Association on why, h=
ow and what it does to support the future of the Drupal project.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>As the Drupal project has grown and changed over the last 20 years, the =
organisation supporting Drupal.org has changed as well. This session offers=
 the chance to hear about some of the various initiatives the Drupal Associ=
ation has been working on and ask questions. The panel includes Drupal Asso=
ciation Board members Audra Martin Merrick, Badd=C3=BD Sonja Breidert and M=
ichel van Velde as well as Rachel Lawson, the Drupal Association community =
Liaison staff member. This AMA (ask me anything) session invites attendees =
to ask about topics they=E2=80=99re concerned about including the effort to=
 run and grow the Drupal project, the decision to change the community elec=
tion process, or any questions around strategic direction. If you have an o=
pinion on how Drupal is supported, this is a great opportunity to ask your =
questions and to help create mutual understanding.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>This session will be moderated by Bert Boerland to ensure a constructive=
 and fruitful dialogue.</p>

         =20
 =20

      </div>
  <div class=3D"session--video">
      </div>
</article>

    </li>
      <li>
     =20
<article role=3D"article" class=3D"node node--type--session node--view-mode=
--embed">
  <div class=3D"session--content">
   =20
    <h3><span class=3D"field field--name-title field--type-string field--la=
bel-hidden">How to create a human culture in a software company</span>
</h3>
   =20
   =20

 =20
 =20
                  <p>In this talk Badd=C3=BD will go over the importance of=
 creating a business environment where all employees are encouraged to find=
 their strength by both growing individually and at the same time contribut=
e outside of the company.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>At 1xINTERNET the management has never been afraid to give people opport=
unities built on their strengths and wishes, and even though it takes some =
effort Baddy believes people should have meaningful purpose during their wo=
rk hours.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>Hear Baddy=C2=B4s stories about the accountant and the engineer that bec=
ame Front Enders at 1xINTERNET and why diversity and flexibility is so impo=
rtant when building a business.</p>

         =20
 =20

      </div>
  <div class=3D"session--video">
      </div>
</article>

    </li>
    </ul>
